WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:05.210
Speaker 1: OK, today we're going to look at
a super interesting interview with a Republican

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:10.820
senator actually being forced to go beyond
the talking points when questioned by Fox

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.019
News host Chris Wallace.

00:00:13.019 --> 00:00:18.480
It's really easy to simply say, you know,
we can increase the deficit.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:21.500
We don't have the money for things Democrats
want to do.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.340
Where is the money going to come from now?

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:26.070
Of course, we know that they never asked those
questions.

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:29.479
When it's about defense spending or war or
tax cuts for the rich, we know about that

00:00:29.479 --> 00:00:30.649
double standard.

00:00:30.649 --> 00:00:35.080
But it doesn't matter because if they're not
questioned about those talking points, there

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:36.719
are lots of people who buy it.

00:00:36.719 --> 00:00:37.719
Hey, yeah.

00:00:37.719 --> 00:00:38.719
Billions, hundreds of billions.

00:00:38.719 --> 00:00:39.940
That sounds crazy.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:42.109
How do we afford this stuff?

00:00:42.109 --> 00:00:46.280
And if they're not questioned about it, they
never really have to explain what they mean.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:49.890
And you get a lot of Republican voters who
end up agreeing with you.

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:56.421
Now, similarly, when Republicans say Biden's
infrastructure plan is too expensive, it's

00:00:56.421 --> 00:00:58.390
not all really infrastructure.

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:00.109
It's filled with crap.

00:01:00.109 --> 00:01:06.800
When they say Biden's job plan is just spending
money we don't have, it's easy as long as

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.880
you never have to explain anything.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:14.729
But when you do have to explain, well, OK,
which of these things would you cut?

00:01:14.729 --> 00:01:19.310
Which of these are not worthy elements for
this plan?

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:21.000
Something interesting happens.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.460
First of all, they almost never have actual
answers.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:29.759
And secondly, it throws them off so badly
that they often end up exposing other garbage

00:01:29.759 --> 00:01:33.420
talking points that they also typically are
allowed to get away with.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:34.610
So let's dove right in.

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:39.159
This is Fox host Chris Wallace asking Republican
Senator Bill Cassidy.

00:01:39.159 --> 00:01:41.340
All right, Senator.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:46.150
Sir, which specific parts of the Biden jobs
plan would you cut?

00:01:46.150 --> 00:01:50.649
There's workforce development, there's childcare,
you know, all these different elements of

00:01:50.649 --> 00:01:51.649
it.

00:01:51.649 --> 00:01:56.900
Cassidy has no answers and instead just starts
slamming teachers unions and it starts to

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:57.900
get pretty unhinged.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.909
Take a look
Speaker 4: up on the screen.

00:01:59.909 --> 00:02:03.070
One hundred billion dollars for workforce
development.

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:06.659
Four hundred billion dollars to care for the
elderly and disabled.

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:09.970
Two hundred and twenty five dollars billion
for child care.

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:12.700
And two hundred dollars billion for free preschool.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:13.760
Senator.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:18.300
Which of those programs that I just put up,
which are those programs do you think people

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:21.550
in your state don't need?

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:24.570
Every one of those programs should be evaluated
if it's important.

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:26.740
It should be advanced, it's not infrastructure.

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:31.860
When people say, wait a second, I like this
because we need a new bridge across the Calcasieu

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:33.390
River in Lake Charles.

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:36.510
I'm saying this plan will not give it to you.

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:42.040
The amount of spending for roads and bridges
is so low that and split between 50 states

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:43.650
over five years.

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:45.690
You're not going to get your bridge now.

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:47.650
We may need this, by the way.

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:54.830
We just are restarting our are bipartisan
working group to come out family support for

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:57.590
the dependent children and elderly.

00:02:57.590 --> 00:03:00.030
But that is not going to give you a road and
bridge.

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:02.330
And that's what people in my state would really
like to see.

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:08.240
Speaker 1: OK, so so far, he doesn't say any
of the programs are bad, but he says they're

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:09.260
not infrastructure.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:10.710
But again, this is a jobs plan.

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:16.840
They're all job related and they are, you
know, education, developing a workforce.

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:21.800
These are even, I would argue, parts of infrastructure
in the 21st century.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:28.280
But then Cassidy says, well, this won't get
my constituents all the things they want.

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:31.410
This money is going to go to all 50 states.

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:37.950
That's not really a reason to oppose the bill
unless your expectation is that all the money

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:38.950
goes to your state.

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:41.360
But that's not how federal spending works.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:42.700
And it's not infrastructure.

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:44.120
But again, it's a jobs bill.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:48.620
So so far, this is the lightest questioning
in other countries.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:53.940
You would be ridiculed as a journalist if
you didn't ask these questions.

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:59.160
And in the United States, with these unprepared
buffoons, just asking the obvious questions

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:01.000
